# Sentinel option 3 targets, installed as /etc/sentinel/targets with mode 0600.
# One container per line, by name or ID. Blank lines and # comments are ignored.
#
#   container <name>   fails unless Status=running and the healthcheck, if
#                      any, is not unhealthy. With auto-recovery on, a
#                      crashed container gets `start` and an unhealthy one
#                      gets `restart`; a container stopped on purpose (exit
#                      code 0, 137 or 143 without OOM) is left alone.
#
# Validate after editing: sudo /usr/local/sbin/sentinel check-config
#
# container web
# container db
